            <ArticleTitle>Self-delivered home-based mirror therapy for lower limb phantom pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>78-81</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/PHM.0b013e318191105b</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Home-based patient-delivered mirror therapy is a promising approach in the treatment of phantom limb pain. Previous studies and case reports of mirror therapy have used a therapist-guided, structured protocol of exercises. No case report has described treatment for either upper or lower limb phantom pain by using home-based patient-delivered mirror therapy. The success of this case demonstrates that home-based patient-delivered mirror therapy may be an efficacious, low-cost treatment option that would eliminate many traditional barriers to care.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
